@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-calendar`

-- ca-tests-commencement.l4
--
-- Sections 5, 6, 7, 18(3), 23 and 2(1) "regulation": the day, and the moment within the day, from which an enactment binds.
-- Expected values written from the text before the module was run (NOTES.md, section 4.2 records the three worked cases).
-- The text keys commencement to the day of ASSENT (ss 5(1), 5(2), 6(2)(a)), not to the day an Act is passed or published.

GIVEN assent IS A DATE
      says IS A `What an enactment says about when it comes into force`
GIVETH A `Commencement facts of an Act`
`an Act assented to on` assent `that` says MEANS
    `Commencement facts of an Act`
        WITH `the day the Act was assented to` IS assent
             `what the provision says about when it comes into force` IS says

GIVEN made IS A DATE
      says IS A `What an enactment says about when it comes into force`
      registered IS A MAYBE DATE
      exempt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Commencement facts of a regulation`
`a regulation made on` made `that` says `registered on` registered `and exempt is` exempt MEANS
    `Commencement facts of a regulation`
        WITH `the day the regulation was made` IS made
             `what the regulation says about when it comes into force` IS says
             `the day it was registered under section 6 of the Statutory Instruments Act, if it has been` IS registered
             `it is of a class exempted from the application of subsection 5(1) of that Act` IS exempt

§ `Worked case 1: an Act assented to on 2026-03-10 that says nothing about its commencement (s 5(2), s 6(2)(a))`

-- The date of commencement is the date of assent (s 5(2)).
#ASSERT `the date of commencement of an Act that provides none, assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
-- It is in force on the expiration of the day immediately before the day of assent (s 6(2)(a)): the expiration of 9 March.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day`) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9))
-- That is the first moment of 10 March.
#ASSERT `the day from which it binds` (`the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day`)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the commencement of an enactment that comes into force as` (`the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day`)) EQUALS `the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT `two moments are the same instant` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9)) `and` (`the commencement of` (YMD 2026 3 10))
-- In force on the 10th and after, not on the 9th.
#ASSERT `an enactment in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9)) `is in force on` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT `an enactment in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9)) `is in force on` (YMD 2026 3 11)
#ASSERT NOT (`an enactment in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9)) `is in force on` (YMD 2026 3 9))
-- The same moment is not the expiration of the 10th.
#ASSERT NOT (`two moments are the same instant` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `and` (`the commencement of` (YMD 2026 3 10)))
-- Across a month end and a year end.
#ASSERT `the day from which it binds` (`the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `that` `it names no day`)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `that` `it names no day`) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2025 12 31))
-- Section 5(3): a provision that the Act is to come into force on a later day is itself deemed in force on the date of assent.
#ASSERT `the moment from which a provision postponing commencement is itself in force, for an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS `the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9)

§ `Worked case 2: an Act that says it comes into force on a day to be fixed later, the day fixed as 2026-06-01 (s 6(1))`

#ASSERT `the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it says the day is to be fixed later` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)))) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 5 31))
#ASSERT `the day from which it binds` (`the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it says the day is to be fixed later` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))))) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
-- 31 May 2026 is a Sunday; the Act is not in force on it, and is in force on Monday 1 June.
#ASSERT NOT (`an enactment in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 5 31)) `is in force on` (YMD 2026 5 31))
#ASSERT `an enactment in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 5 31)) `is in force on` (YMD 2026 6 1)
-- The day is not yet fixed: no day yet decides it.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it says the day is to be fixed later` NOTHING)) EQUALS `there is as yet no day from which it binds`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the day from which it binds` (`the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it says the day is to be fixed later` NOTHING))))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the commencement of an enactment that comes into force as` (`the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it says the day is to be fixed later` NOTHING))))

§ `An Act that names a particular day (s 6(1))`

#ASSERT `the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it names a particular day` (YMD 2026 4 1))) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 31))
#ASSERT `the day from which it binds` (`the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it names a particular day` (YMD 2026 4 1)))) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1
-- A particular day that is the day of assent itself.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it names a particular day` (YMD 2026 3 10))) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9))

§ `An enactment expressed to expire, lapse or cease to have effect on a particular day (s 6(1))`

-- It ceases to have effect on the commencement of the following day: the whole of the named day is still inside it.
#ASSERT `the moment of ceasing to have effect of an enactment expressed to expire on` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS `the commencement of` (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `an enactment that ceases to have effect at` (`the commencement of` (YMD 2027 1 1)) `is still in force on` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`an enactment that ceases to have effect at` (`the commencement of` (YMD 2027 1 1)) `is still in force on` (YMD 2027 1 1))
#ASSERT `the moment of ceasing to have effect of an enactment expressed to expire on` (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS `the commencement of` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `the moment of ceasing to have effect of an enactment expressed to expire on` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS `the commencement of` (YMD 2024 2 29)

§ `Worked case 3: subordinate legislation made on 2026-03-10 that says nothing about when it comes into force (s 6(2)(b))`

-- Of a class exempted from subsection 5(1) of the Statutory Instruments Act: the expiration of the day before the day it was made.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of a regulation` (`a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day` `registered on` NOTHING `and exempt is` TRUE) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9))
-- Not exempt, registered on 12 March: the expiration of the day before the day it was registered.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of a regulation` (`a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day` `registered on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 12)) `and exempt is` FALSE) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 11))
#ASSERT `the day from which it binds` (`the coming into force of a regulation` (`a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day` `registered on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 12)) `and exempt is` FALSE)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 12
-- Registered the day it was made.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of a regulation` (`a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day` `registered on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `and exempt is` FALSE) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9))
-- Not exempt and not yet registered: the text gives the registration day as the pivot, so no day yet decides it.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of a regulation` (`a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day` `registered on` NOTHING `and exempt is` FALSE) EQUALS `there is as yet no day from which it binds`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the day from which it binds` (`the coming into force of a regulation` (`a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day` `registered on` NOTHING `and exempt is` FALSE)))
-- A regulation that names its own day: s 6(1) governs, whatever the registration.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of a regulation` (`a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it names a particular day` (YMD 2026 4 15)) `registered on` NOTHING `and exempt is` FALSE) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 4 14))
-- A regulation whose day is to be fixed later.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of a regulation` (`a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it says the day is to be fixed later` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))) `registered on` NOTHING `and exempt is` FALSE) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 5 31))
#ASSERT `the coming into force of a regulation` (`a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` (`it says the day is to be fixed later` NOTHING) `registered on` NOTHING `and exempt is` FALSE) EQUALS `there is as yet no day from which it binds`

§ `Section 6(3): judicial notice of a day fixed by a regulation`

#ASSERT `judicial notice shall be taken of the day` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`judicial notice shall be taken of the day` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`judicial notice shall be taken of the day` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`judicial notice shall be taken of the day` FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 7: power exercised before commencement`

-- The enactment is first in force on 1 April; on 30 March the regulation made beforehand has effect only so far as necessary.
#ASSERT `a regulation made or a thing done before commencement has effect on` (YMD 2026 3 30) `where the enactment is first in force on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `and` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a regulation made or a thing done before commencement has effect on` (YMD 2026 3 30) `where the enactment is first in force on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a regulation made or a thing done before commencement has effect on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `where the enactment is first in force on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `and` FALSE
#ASSERT `a regulation made or a thing done before commencement has effect on` (YMD 2026 4 2) `where the enactment is first in force on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `and` FALSE

§ `Section 18(3): when a proclamation takes effect`

-- It may purport to have been issued on the day of the order or on any subsequent day, and then takes effect on that day.
#ASSERT `the day a proclamation takes effect, issued under an order of` (YMD 2026 3 10) `purporting to be issued on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the day a proclamation takes effect, issued under an order of` (YMD 2026 3 10) `purporting to be issued on` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the day a proclamation takes effect, issued under an order of` (YMD 2026 3 10) `purporting to be issued on` (YMD 2026 3 9))

§ `Section 23: when an appointment takes effect`

-- (2): an instrument under the Great Seal may purport to be issued on or after the day its issue was authorized.
#ASSERT `the day an appointment under the Great Seal takes effect, issue authorized on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `purporting to be issued on` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the day an appointment under the Great Seal takes effect, issue authorized on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `purporting to be issued on` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the day an appointment under the Great Seal takes effect, issue authorized on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `purporting to be issued on` (YMD 2026 2 28))
-- (3): the expressed day is deemed the day of effect unless it is MORE THAN sixty days before the day of issue.
-- Duties began 1 January; expressed effective 1 January; issued 2 March is exactly 60 days later (31 + 28 + 1): inside.
#ASSERT `the day an appointment otherwise than under the Great Seal takes effect, duties begun on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `expressed effective on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `issued on` (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
-- Issued 3 March is 61 days later: more than sixty.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the day an appointment otherwise than under the Great Seal takes effect, duties begun on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `expressed effective on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `issued on` (YMD 2026 3 3))
-- Expressed effective before the duties began is not within the subsection.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the day an appointment otherwise than under the Great Seal takes effect, duties begun on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `expressed effective on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15))
-- Expressed effective after the duties began and well within sixty days.
#ASSERT `the day an appointment otherwise than under the Great Seal takes effect, duties begun on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `expressed effective on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `issued on` (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
-- (5): effective on a specified day is deemed effected immediately on the expiration of the previous day.
#ASSERT `the moment an appointment or a termination is deemed to take effect, if it is effective on` (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS `the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `the moment an appointment or a termination is deemed to take effect, if it is effective on` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS `the expiration of` (YMD 2026 2 28)

§ `Section 2(1) "regulation"`

#ASSERT `is a regulation` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `is a regulation` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `is a regulation` TRUE TRUE
-- An instrument issued under neither limb: the definition says what a regulation includes, not what it excludes.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`is a regulation` FALSE FALSE)
